<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 30-APR.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 30-APR.</headline>
<text>
<p>Flood crests continue to move northward along the Red River in southern Manitoba, Canada, and should reach Winnepeg later in the week, resulting in the worst flooding in years there. Rivers continue to recede slowly in and around the areas of Grand Forks and Fargo, North Dakota, with slow improvement. Generally dry with just a few light showers today-Thursday through the flooded areas. There may be moderate rain Friday, which will aggrivate flooding somewhat, if it occurs.</p>
</text>
